{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/544357-using-dominate-on-other-supernaturals","id":544357,"title":"Using Dominate on Other supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-07T15:59:43-07:00","id":544357,"title":"Using Dominate on Other supernaturals","content":"So I'm in a game with mixed supernaturals, and of course one of the vampires is a ventrue, and of course he's focusing on dominate because that's just what they do. In the Requiem books, it says you add your blood potency to your resolve to determine your die pool to resist getting dominated (and a bunch of other disciplines at that). My question is if you used Dominate or a similar power on a different supernatural, would they get to add their template's equivalent to their die pool (A werewolf would add his primal urge for example)? I'd rather have an answer now than have to look it up when he inevitably tries to dominate something that isn't a vampire or a vanilla mortal","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:04:31-07:00","id":544379,"title":"","content":"Yes. In any instances where it says Blood Potency, with other supernaturals, just replace it with their Supernatural Advantage, which is Primal Urge, Gnosis, etc. etc.<br /> <br /> The one exception sort of is Demons, who instead contest with their Cover rating if they're in Cover instead of their Primum (Use Primum if they're in their Demonic Form.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T16:38:43-07:00","id":544473,"title":"","content":"BP = supernatural tolerance, Like Leetsepeak already said. And anything that tries to effect him supernaturaly he would get to add his BP to whatever.<br /> <br /> I would just like to add If you decided to roll in Beasts(with the preview out) in this Crossover Lair would be the supernatural tolerance for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5950-mal","name":"Mal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5950_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-07T20:19:07-07:00","id":544689,"title":"","content":"For your benefit, this is covered on page 125 of Vampire: the Requiem Second Edition, under the heading &quot;Supernatural Conflict.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you want to have a quote from the rulebook to back you up in case of player's disagreeing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}